<section>
<section id="details-on-ecc" class="title-slide slide level1">
<h1>Details on ECC</h1>

</section>
<section class="slide level2">
<h2>ECC adding: real and in <span
class="math inline">E_{p}(a,b)</span></h2>
<div class="dada-frame-body">
<div class="block">
<div class="block-title block-title-hfill">
<span class="block-title-left">Adding points in <span
class="math inline">E(a,b)</span></span><span
class="block-title-right">(Real curve)</span>
</div>
<div class="block-content">
<div class="dada-font-footnotesize">
<p>If we had<span style="color: blue"> <span
class="math inline">P=(x_{P},y_{P})</span> </span> and<span
style="color: blue"> <span
class="math inline">Q=(x_{Q},y_{Q})</span></span>, and<span
style="color: blue"> <span class="math inline">P\neq\pm Q</span></span>.
We can find<span style="color: blue"> <span
class="math inline">R=P+_{E(a,b)}Q</span></span> by finding <span
style="color: blue">gradient</span> of line, and then <span
style="color: blue">intersection</span> with curve:</p>
</div>
<div class="center">
<div class="dada-font-footnotesize">
<p><span class="roman"> </span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div class="center">
<div class="dada-font-footnotesize">
<div class="dada-fbox dada-font-footnotesize"
style="width: 50%; border: 2px solid black; background-color: white; box-sizing: border-box;">
<table>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td style="text-align: right;"><span
class="dada-font-footnotesize">Gradient:</span></td>
<td style="text-align: left;"><span class="dada-font-footnotesize"><span
style="color: blue"><span
class="math inline">\Delta=\frac{y_{Q}-y_{P}}{x_{Q}-x_{P}}</span></span></span></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td style="text-align: right;"><span
class="dada-font-footnotesize"><span class="math inline">x</span>
coordinate for <span class="math inline">R</span>:</span></td>
<td style="text-align: left;"><span class="dada-font-footnotesize"><span
style="color: blue"><span
class="math inline">x_{R}=\Delta^{2}-x_{P}-x_{Q}</span></span></span></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td style="text-align: right;"><span
class="dada-font-footnotesize"><span class="math inline">y</span>
coordinate for <span class="math inline">R</span>:</span></td>
<td style="text-align: left;"><span class="dada-font-footnotesize"><span
style="color: blue"><span
class="math inline">y_{R}=\Delta(x_{P}-x_{R})-y_{P}</span></span></span></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td style="text-align: right;"><span
class="dada-font-footnotesize">Finally:</span></td>
<td style="text-align: left;"><span class="dada-font-footnotesize"><span
style="color: blue"><span
class="math inline">R=(x_{R},y_{R})</span></span></span></td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="dada-font-footnotesize">
<p><span style="color: blue"><span
class="math inline">P+_{E(a,b)}P</span></span> uses a different
method.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="exampleblock">
<div class="block-title block-title-hfill">
<span class="block-title-left">Adding points in <span
class="math inline">E_{p}(a,b)</span>: (modulo p)</span><span
class="block-title-right">(Finite field)</span>
</div>
<div class="block-content">
<div class="center">
<div class="dada-font-footnotesize">
<div class="dada-fbox dada-font-footnotesize"
style="width: 55%; border: 2px solid black; background-color: white; box-sizing: border-box;">
<table>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td style="text-align: right;"><span
class="dada-font-footnotesize">Gradient:</span></td>
<td style="text-align: left;"><span class="dada-font-footnotesize"><span
style="color: blue"><span
class="math inline">\Delta=\frac{y_{Q}-y_{P}}{x_{Q}-x_{P}}\bmod
p</span></span></span></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td style="text-align: right;"><span
class="dada-font-footnotesize"><span class="math inline">x</span>
coordinate for <span class="math inline">R</span>:</span></td>
<td style="text-align: left;"><span class="dada-font-footnotesize"><span
style="color: blue"><span
class="math inline">x_{R}=\Delta^{2}-x_{P}-x_{Q}\bmod
p</span></span></span></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td style="text-align: right;"><span
class="dada-font-footnotesize"><span class="math inline">y</span>
coordinate for <span class="math inline">R</span>:</span></td>
<td style="text-align: left;"><span class="dada-font-footnotesize"><span
style="color: blue"><span
class="math inline">y_{R}=\Delta(x_{P}-x_{R})-y_{P}\bmod
p</span></span></span></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td style="text-align: right;"><span
class="dada-font-footnotesize">Finally:</span></td>
<td style="text-align: left;"><span class="dada-font-footnotesize"><span
style="color: blue"><span
class="math inline">R=(x_{R},y_{R})</span></span></span></td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="dada-font-footnotesize">
<p><span style="color: blue"><span
class="math inline">P+_{E_{p}(a,b)}P</span></span> again uses the
different method.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section class="slide level2">
<h2>Curve <span class="math inline">y^{2}=x^{3}+x+1\bmod23</span> does
not “look” nice</h2>
<div class="dada-frame-body">
<div class="center">
<div class="image-grid">
<img data-src="../../images/ECC1.png" style="max-width: none; width: auto; height:4.5cm"
alt="image" />
<img data-src="../../images/ECC2.png" style="max-width: none; width: auto; height:4.5cm"
alt="image" />
</div>
</div>
<div class="exampleblock">
<div class="block-title">
Example <span class="math inline">P+_{E_{23}(1,1)}Q</span> operations
</div>
<div class="block-content">
<div class="center">
<div class="dada-fbox"
style="width: 72%; border: 2px solid black; background-color: white; box-sizing: border-box;">
<div class="table-with-borders">
<table>
<thead>
<tr style="background-color: rgb(0,255,255);">
<th style="text-align: center;"><span class="dada-font-tiny"><span
class="dada-bold"><span
style="color: blue">P+Q</span></span></span></th>
<th style="border-right: none; text-align: left;"><span class="dada-font-tiny"><span
class="dada-bold"><span style="color: blue">Gradient <span
class="math inline">\Delta</span></span></span></span></th>
<th style="border-left: none; border-right: none; text-align: left;"><span class="dada-font-tiny"><span
class="dada-bold"><span style="color: blue">x coordinate <span
class="math inline">x_{R}</span></span></span></span></th>
<th style="border-left: none; text-align: center;"><span class="dada-font-tiny"><span
class="dada-bold"><span style="color: blue">y coordinate <span
class="math inline">y_{R}</span></span></span></span></th>
<th style="text-align: center;"><span class="dada-font-tiny"><span
class="dada-bold"><span style="color: blue">R</span></span></span></th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td style="text-align: center;"><span class="dada-font-tiny"><span
style="color: blue"><span
class="math inline">(3,10)+(9,7)</span></span></span></td>
<td style="border-right: none; text-align: left;"><span class="dada-font-tiny"><span
style="color: blue"><span
class="math inline">=\frac{-3}{6}=11</span></span></span></td>
<td style="border-left: none; border-right: none; text-align: left;"><span class="dada-font-tiny"><span
style="color: blue"><span
class="math inline">=11^{2}-3-9=17</span></span></span></td>
<td style="border-left: none; text-align: left;"><span class="dada-font-tiny"><span
style="color: blue"><span
class="math inline">=11(3-17)-10=20</span></span></span></td>
<td style="text-align: center;"><span class="dada-font-tiny"><span
style="color: blue"><span
class="math inline">(17,20)</span></span></span></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td style="text-align: center;"><span class="dada-font-tiny"><span
style="color: blue"><span
class="math inline">(4,0)+(7,11)</span></span></span></td>
<td style="border-right: none; text-align: left;"><span class="dada-font-tiny"><span
style="color: blue"><span
class="math inline">=\frac{11}{3}=19</span></span></span></td>
<td style="border-left: none; border-right: none; text-align: left;"><span class="dada-font-tiny"><span
style="color: blue"><span
class="math inline">=19^{2}-4-7=5</span></span></span></td>
<td style="border-left: none; text-align: left;"><span class="dada-font-tiny"><span
style="color: blue"><span
class="math inline">=19(4-5)-0=4</span></span></span></td>
<td style="text-align: center;"><span class="dada-font-tiny"><span
style="color: blue"><span
class="math inline">(5,4)</span></span></span></td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section class="slide level2">
<h2>Calculating <span class="math inline">2P=P+_{E_{P}(a,b)}P</span> for
ECC</h2>
<div class="dada-frame-body">
<div class="block">
<div class="block-title">
Doubling a point in <span class="math inline">\left\langle
+_{E_{p}(a,b)},E_{p}(a,b)\right\rangle</span>
</div>
<div class="block-content">
<ul>
<li><span class="dada-font-footnotesize">If <span
style="color: blue"><span class="math inline">y_{P}=0</span></span>,
return <span style="color: blue"><span
class="math inline">O</span></span>, the zero point.</span></li>
<li><span class="dada-font-footnotesize"><span style="color: blue"><span
class="math inline">P=(x_{P},y_{P})</span></span>, and<span
style="color: blue"> <span
class="math inline">y_{P}\neq0</span></span>.</span></li>
<li><span class="dada-font-footnotesize">Find<span style="color: blue">
<span class="math inline">R=P+_{E_{p}(a,b)}P</span></span> by finding
<span style="color: blue">gradient</span> of the <span
style="color: blue">tangent</span>, and then <span
style="color: blue">intersection</span> with curve:</span></li>
</ul>
<div class="center">
<div class="dada-font-footnotesize">
<p><span class="roman"> </span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div class="center">
<div class="dada-font-footnotesize">
<div class="dada-fbox dada-font-footnotesize"
style="width: 55%; border: 2px solid black; background-color: white; box-sizing: border-box;">
<table>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td style="text-align: right;"><span
class="dada-font-footnotesize">Gradient:</span></td>
<td style="text-align: left;"><span class="dada-font-footnotesize"><span
style="color: blue"><span
class="math inline">\Delta=\frac{3x_{P}^{2}+a}{2y_{P}}\bmod
p</span></span></span></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td style="text-align: right;"><span
class="dada-font-footnotesize"><span class="math inline">x</span>
coordinate for <span class="math inline">R</span>:</span></td>
<td style="text-align: left;"><span class="dada-font-footnotesize"><span
style="color: blue"><span
class="math inline">x_{R}=\Delta^{2}-2x_{P}\bmod
p</span></span></span></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td style="text-align: right;"><span
class="dada-font-footnotesize"><span class="math inline">y</span>
coordinate for <span class="math inline">R</span>:</span></td>
<td style="text-align: left;"><span class="dada-font-footnotesize"><span
style="color: blue"><span
class="math inline">y_{R}=\Delta(x_{P}-x_{R})-y_{P}\bmod
p</span></span></span></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td style="text-align: right;"><span
class="dada-font-footnotesize">Finally:</span></td>
<td style="text-align: left;"><span class="dada-font-footnotesize"><span
style="color: blue"><span
class="math inline">R=(x_{R},y_{R})</span></span></span></td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="exampleblock">
<div class="block-title">
All operations modulo 23...
</div>
<div class="block-content">
<div class="center">
<div class="dada-fbox"
style="width: 71%; border: 2px solid black; background-color: white; box-sizing: border-box;">
<div class="table-with-borders">
<table>
<thead>
<tr style="background-color: rgb(0,255,255);">
<th style="text-align: center;"><span class="dada-font-tiny"><span
class="dada-bold"><span
style="color: blue">P+P</span></span></span></th>
<th style="border-right: none; text-align: left;"><span class="dada-font-tiny"><span
class="dada-bold"><span style="color: blue">Gradient <span
class="math inline">\Delta</span></span></span></span></th>
<th style="border-left: none; border-right: none; text-align: left;"><span class="dada-font-tiny"><span
class="dada-bold"><span style="color: blue">x coordinate <span
class="math inline">x_{R}</span></span></span></span></th>
<th style="border-left: none; text-align: center;"><span class="dada-font-tiny"><span
class="dada-bold"><span style="color: blue">y coordinate <span
class="math inline">y_{R}</span></span></span></span></th>
<th style="text-align: center;"><span class="dada-font-tiny"><span
class="dada-bold"><span style="color: blue">R</span></span></span></th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td style="text-align: center;"><span class="dada-font-tiny"><span
style="color: blue"><span
class="math inline">(7,11)+(7,11)</span></span></span></td>
<td style="border-right: none; text-align: left;"><span class="dada-font-tiny"><span
style="color: blue"><span
class="math inline">=\frac{10}{22}=13</span></span></span></td>
<td style="border-left: none; border-right: none; text-align: left;"><span class="dada-font-tiny"><span
style="color: blue"><span
class="math inline">=13^{2}-14=17</span></span></span></td>
<td style="border-left: none; text-align: left;"><span class="dada-font-tiny"><span
style="color: blue"><span
class="math inline">=13(7-17)-11=20</span></span></span></td>
<td style="text-align: center;"><span class="dada-font-tiny"><span
style="color: blue"><span
class="math inline">(17,20)</span></span></span></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td style="text-align: center;"><span class="dada-font-tiny"><span
style="color: blue"><span
class="math inline">(9,7)+(9,7)</span></span></span></td>
<td style="border-right: none; text-align: left;"><span class="dada-font-tiny"><span
style="color: blue"><span
class="math inline">=\frac{14}{14}=1</span></span></span></td>
<td style="border-left: none; border-right: none; text-align: left;"><span class="dada-font-tiny"><span
style="color: blue"><span
class="math inline">=1^{2}-18=6</span></span></span></td>
<td style="border-left: none; text-align: left;"><span class="dada-font-tiny"><span
style="color: blue"><span
class="math inline">=1(9-6)-7=19</span></span></span></td>
<td style="text-align: center;"><span class="dada-font-tiny"><span
style="color: blue"><span
class="math inline">(6,19)</span></span></span></td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section class="slide level2">
<h2>On <span class="math inline">\frac{a}{b}\bmod p</span> calculation
for ECC</h2>
<div class="dada-frame-body">
<div class="block">
<div class="block-title">
Dividing by <span class="math inline">b</span> is the same as
multiplication by <span class="math inline">b^{-1}</span>:
</div>
<div class="block-content">
<div class="dada-font-footnotesize">
<p>To calculate<span style="color: blue"> <span
class="math inline">\frac{a}{b}\bmod p</span></span>,</p>
</div>
<ol>
<li><span class="dada-font-footnotesize">Use extended euclidean
algorithm to calculate <span style="color: blue"><span
class="math inline">b^{-1}\bmod p</span></span>.</span></li>
<li><span class="dada-font-footnotesize">Then multiply<span
style="color: blue"> <span class="math inline">a\times b^{-1}\bmod
p</span></span>.</span></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
<div class="exampleblock">
<div class="block-title">
All operations modulo 23...
</div>
<div class="block-content">
<div class="dada-font-footnotesize">
<p>To calculate<span style="color: blue"> <span
class="math inline">\frac{7}{11}\bmod23</span></span></p>
</div>
<ol>
<li><span class="dada-font-footnotesize">Calculate<span
style="color: blue"> <span
class="math inline">11^{-1}\bmod23=21</span></span>.</span></li>
<li><span class="dada-font-footnotesize"><span style="color: blue"><span
class="math inline">7\times21\bmod23=9</span></span></span></li>
</ol>
<div class="dada-font-tiny">
<p><a
href="https://nvlpubs.nist.gov/nistpubs/SpecialPublications/NIST.SP.800-57pt1r5.pdf"
class="uri">https://nvlpubs.nist.gov/nistpubs/SpecialPublications/NIST.SP.800-57pt1r5.pdf</a></p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</section></section>
<section>
<section
id="building-blocks-for-hardness-operations-in-mathbbz_p-and-mathbbz_n"
class="title-slide slide level1">
<h1>Building blocks for “hardness” operations in <span
class="math inline">\mathbb{Z}_{p}</span> and <span
class="math inline">\mathbb{Z}_{N}</span> </h1>

</section>
<section class="slide level2">
<h2>Outline</h2>
<div class="dada-frame-body">
<div class="dada-toc">
<ol>
<li><span style="color: lightgray">Details on ECC</span></li>
<li><span style="color: blue"><span class="dada-bold">Building blocks
for “hardness” operations in <span
class="math inline">\mathbb{Z}_{p}</span> and <span
class="math inline">\mathbb{Z}_{N}</span></span> </span>
<ul>
<li><span class="dada-bold">Cyclic groups, math
operations...</span></li>
<li><span style="color: lightgray">Algorithms, with
complexity</span></li>
<li><span style="color: lightgray">Problems in <span
class="math inline">\mathbb{Z}_{p}</span> and <span
class="math inline">\mathbb{Z}_{N}</span> </span></li>
</ul></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section class="slide level2">
<h2>Abstract algebra concepts...</h2>
<div class="dada-frame-body">
<div class="center">
<div class="dada-fbox"
style="width: 70%; border: 2px solid black; background-color: white; box-sizing: border-box;">
<img data-src="../../images/FieldsRingsAndGroups.png"
style="height: auto; width:100.0%" alt="image" />
</div>
</div>
<div class="block">
<div class="block-title">
Fields, rings and groups
</div>
<div class="block-content">
<div class="dada-font-footnotesize">
<p><span style="color: black">In crypto, we often work with finite,
cyclic mathematical structures. These have been studied for centuries,
and it is appropriate for us to know about the mathematical domain in
which we must work.</span></p>
</div>
<div class="dada-font-footnotesize">
<p><span style="color: black">I say <span class="dada-emph"><span
style="color: black">must</span></span>, because without knowing the
hard facts/limits of the mathematical structures we must deal with, we
have <span class="dada-emph"><span
style="color: black">nothing</span></span> (!)</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section class="slide level2">
<h2><span class="math inline">17^{\mathrm{th}}</span> century Frenchman
Pierre de Fermat<img data-src="../../images/Zp.png" style="max-width: none; width: auto; height:0.3cm"
alt="image" /></h2>
<div class="dada-frame-body">
<div class="block">
<div class="block-title block-title-hfill">
<span class="block-title-left">Fermat’s (little) theorem for <span
class="math inline">\mathbb{Z}_{p}</span>:</span><span
class="block-title-right">(primes)</span>
</div>
<div class="block-content">
<div class="dada-font-footnotesize dada-hfill-layout">
When<span style="color: blue"> <span class="math inline">p</span></span>
is a prime<span style="color: black">, if</span><span
style="color: blue"> <span class="math inline">a</span> </span><span
style="color: black">is any non-zero number less than </span><span
style="color: blue"><span class="math inline">p</span></span><span
style="color: black">, then </span>
<div class="dada-fbox"
style="width: 17%; border: 2px solid black; background-color: white; box-sizing: border-box;">
<div class="center">
<p><span style="color: blue"><span class="math inline">{a^{p-1}\bmod
p=1}</span></span></p>
</div>
</div>
<span style="color: black">.</span>
</div>
<div class="dada-font-footnotesize">
<hr style="border: none; border-top: 3px solid black; width: 100%; margin: 0.4em 0;">
</div>
