<section class="slide level2">
<h2>Leonhard Euler (1707-1783)</h2>
<div class="dada-frame-body">
<div class="center">
<table>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td style="text-align: center;"><img
data-src="../../images/Euler1707-1783.png" style="height: auto; width:100.0%"
alt="image" />  </td>
<td style="text-align: center;">  <img
data-src="../../images/MeAndMyMateEuler.png" style="height: auto; width:100.0%"
alt="image" /></td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section class="slide level2">
<h2>Euler’s theorem - a generalization of Fermat’s<img
data-src="../../images/ZN.png" style="max-width: none; width: auto; height:0.3cm" alt="image" /></h2>
<div class="dada-frame-body">
<div class="block">
<div class="block-title block-title-hfill">
<span class="block-title-left">Euler’s theorem:</span><span
class="block-title-right">(composites)</span>
</div>
<div class="block-content">
<div class="dada-font-footnotesize">
<p><span style="color: black">If</span> <span style="color: blue"><span
class="math inline">N</span></span> <span style="color: black">is any
positive integer and</span> <span style="color: blue"><span
class="math inline">a</span></span> <span style="color: black">is any
positive integer less than</span> <span style="color: blue"><span
class="math inline">N</span></span> <span style="color: black">with no
divisors in common with</span> <span style="color: blue"><span
class="math inline">N</span></span><span style="color: black">,
then</span></p>
</div>
<div class="center">
<div class="dada-font-footnotesize">
<p><span class="roman"> </span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div class="center">
<div class="dada-font-footnotesize">
<div class="dada-fbox"
style="width: 20%; border: 2px solid black; background-color: white; box-sizing: border-box;">
<div class="center">
<p><span style="color: blue"><span class="math inline">{a^{\phi(N)}\bmod
N=1}</span></span></p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="dada-font-footnotesize">
<p><span style="color: black">where</span> <span
style="color: blue"><span class="math inline">\phi(N)</span></span>
<span style="color: black">is the</span> <span
style="color: black"><span class="dada-emph">Euler phi (totient)
function</span></span><span style="color: black">:</span></p>
</div>
<div class="center">
<div class="dada-font-footnotesize">
<p><span class="roman"> </span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div class="center">
<div class="dada-font-footnotesize">
<div class="dada-fbox"
style="width: 40%; border: 2px solid black; background-color: white; box-sizing: border-box;">
<div class="center">
<p><span style="color: blue"><span
class="math inline">{\phi(N)=N(1-1/p_{1})\ldots(1-1/p_{m})}</span></span></p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="dada-font-footnotesize">
<p><span style="color: black">and</span> <span style="color: blue"><span
class="math inline">p_{1}</span>, <span
class="math inline">\ldots</span> , <span
class="math inline">p_{m}</span></span> <span style="color: black">are
all the prime numbers that divide evenly into</span> <span
style="color: blue"><span class="math inline">N</span></span><span
style="color: black">. </span></p>
</div>
<div class="dada-font-footnotesize">
<hr style="border: none; border-top: 3px solid black; width: 100%; margin: 0.4em 0;">
</div>
<div class="dada-font-footnotesize">
<p>If <span style="color: blue"><span
class="math inline">N</span></span> <span style="color: black">is a
prime, then using the formula, we have</span></p>
</div>
<div class="center">
<div class="dada-font-footnotesize">
<p><span class="roman"> </span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div class="center">
<div class="dada-font-footnotesize">
<div class="dada-fbox"
style="width: 45%; border: 2px solid black; background-color: white; box-sizing: border-box;">
<div class="center">
<p><span style="color: blue"><span
class="math inline">{\phi(N)=N(1-\frac{1}{N})=N(\frac{N-1}{N})=N-1}</span></span></p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="dada-font-footnotesize">
<p><span style="color: black">We see that Fermat’s result is a</span>
<span style="color: blue">special case</span> <span
style="color: black">of Euler’s:</span></p>
</div>
<div class="center">
<div class="dada-font-footnotesize">
<p><span class="roman"> </span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div class="center">
<div class="dada-font-footnotesize">
<div class="dada-fbox"
style="width: 40%; border: 2px solid black; background-color: white; box-sizing: border-box;">
<div class="center">
<p><span style="color: blue"><span class="math inline">{a^{\phi(N)}\bmod
N=a^{N-1}\bmod N=1}</span></span></p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section class="slide level2">
<h2>Special cases<img data-src="../../images/ZN.png"
style="max-width: none; width: auto; height:0.3cm" alt="image" /></h2>
<div class="dada-frame-body">
<div class="exampleblock">
<div class="block-title block-title-hfill">
<span class="block-title-left">Special case #2</span><span
class="block-title-right">(RSA-style composites)</span>
</div>
<div class="block-content">
<div class="dada-font-footnotesize">
<p>Another <span style="color: blue">special case</span> <span
style="color: black">needed for RSA comes when the modulus is a product
of two (different) primes:</span> <span style="color: blue"><span
class="math inline">N=pq</span></span><span style="color: black">.
Then</span></p>
</div>
<div class="center">
<div class="dada-font-footnotesize">
<p><span class="roman"> </span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div class="center">
<div class="dada-font-footnotesize">
<div class="dada-fbox"
style="width: 45%; border: 2px solid black; background-color: white; box-sizing: border-box;">
<div class="center">
<p><span style="color: blue"><span
class="math inline">{\phi(N)=N(1-\frac{1}{p})(1-\frac{1}{q})=(p-1)(q-1)}</span></span></p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="dada-font-footnotesize">
<p><span style="color: blue">and so we have</span></p>
</div>
<div class="center">
<div class="dada-font-footnotesize">
<p><span class="roman"> </span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div class="center">
<div class="dada-font-footnotesize">
<div class="dada-fbox"
style="width: 25%; border: 2px solid black; background-color: white; box-sizing: border-box;">
<div class="center">
<p><span style="color: blue"><span
class="math inline">{a^{(p-1)(q-1)}\bmod pq=1}</span></span></p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="dada-font-footnotesize">
<p><span style="color: black">(if</span><span style="color: blue"> <span
class="math inline">a</span></span><span style="color: black"> has no
divisors in common with </span><span style="color: blue"><span
class="math inline">pq</span></span><span style="color: black"> and
</span><span style="color: blue"><span
class="math inline">p,q</span></span><span style="color: black">
prime)</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="block">
<div class="block-title">
On the next slide we illustrate Euler with <span
class="math inline">N=15</span>
</div>
<div class="block-content">
<div class="dada-font-footnotesize">
<p>The table illustrates Euler’s theorem for <span
style="color: blue"><span
class="math inline">N=15=3\times5</span></span><span
style="color: black">, with</span></p>
</div>
<div class="center">
<div class="dada-font-footnotesize">
<p><span class="roman"> </span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div class="center">
<div class="dada-font-footnotesize">
<div class="dada-fbox"
style="width: 50%; border: 2px solid black; background-color: white; box-sizing: border-box;">
<div class="center">
<p><span style="color: blue"><span
class="math inline">{\phi(15)=15(1-\frac{1}{3})(1-\frac{1}{5})=(3-1)(5-1)=8}</span></span></p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="dada-font-footnotesize">
<p>Notice here that a <span style="color: blue"><span
class="math inline">1</span></span> is reached when the power is<span
style="color: blue"> <span class="math inline">8</span></span>, but only
for numbers with no divisors in common with <span
style="color: blue"><span class="math inline">15</span></span>.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</section>
